    "ls|LS17_S15_U_103": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nDEPARTMENTOF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 103\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 9TH FEBRUARY, 2024\nHUMAN RESOURCE IN AIIMS\n†*103. SHRI DEEPAK BAIJ:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of employees vis-a-vis doctors, nurses, paramedical and other staff\nworking in All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) operating in the country\nincluding Raipur AIIMS; and\n(b) whether AIIMS operating in the country are functioning to their full capacity\ndespite the lack of human resource therein and if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\n(DR MANSUKH MANDA VIYA)\n(a) & ( b) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENTREFERRED TO IN REPLYTO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 103 FOR 9TH FEBRUARY,2024\n(a): The details of Faculty (doctors) and Non-Faculty (including Nurses, Paramedical\nand other staff) working in All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) in the\ncountry including AIIMS Raipur is at Annexure-I.\n(b): In addition to AIIMS New Delhi, Government has approved setting up of 22\nnew AIIMS under Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana (PMSSY). Balance is\nmaintained between the development of infrastructure and engagement of human\nresources for optimum utilisation of facilities.\n\nAnnexure I\nDetails of Faculty (doctors) and Non-Faculty (inculding SR/JR, Nurses, Paramedical\nand other staff) working in AIIMS\nSl. No. Name of AIIMS Faculty Position Non-Faculty position\n1. New Delhi 834 11124\n2. Bhopal 231 2937\n3. Bhubaneswar 248 2319\n4. Jodhpur 227 2558\n5. Patna 219 2697\n6. Raipur 188 2417\n7. Rishikesh 213 2501\n8. Mangalagiri 133 936\n9. Nagpur 177 981\n10. Kalyani 146 777\n11. Gorakhpur 103 731\n12. Bathinda 147 875\n13. Bilaspur 101 831\n14. Guwahati 93 365\n15. Deoghar 111 763\n16. Bibinagar 106 661\n17. Raebareli 105 895\n18. Rajkot 69 445\n19. Madurai 50 33\n20. Vijaypur Jammu 85 554\n*****",
