    "ls|LS17_S15_U_105": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nDEPARTMENTOF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 105\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02ND FEBRUARY, 2024\nCOLLEGES OF NURSING\n105 : ADV .ADOOR PRAKASH:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of the existing nursing schools upgraded as Colleges of Nursing under\nthe Central Sector Scheme for upgradation;\n(b) the present status of the implementation of the scheme along with the nursing\nschools upgraded so far details, State/UT-wise;\n(c) the details of the pending proposals before the Union Government and the present\nstatus, State/ UT-wise; and\n(d) whether any proposal has been received from the State Government of Kerala for\nupgradation of School of Nursing into College of Nursing since the\nimplementation of the scheme, if so, the details thereof and the status of the\nproposals submitted by the state?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATEIN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH\nAND FAMILYWELFARE\n(Dr. BHARATI PRA VINPAWAR)\n(a) to (d) Under the Central Sector Scheme “Development of Nursing Services”, funds to\nthe tune of Rs.7.00 crore is released for Upgradation of each School of Nursing into\nCollege of Nursing. So far, 48 Institutes have been allocated funds for upgradation of\nSchool of Nursing into College of Nursing. List of these 48 institutions along with\nfunds released so far is at Annexure-I.\n\nAnnexure-I\nS.N\no\nState Name of Institution Fund\nreleased (Rs.\nIn crore)\n1 Gujarat 1. School of Nursing, Sir T. General Hospital, Jail\nRoad, Bhavnagar\n1.025\n2. School of Nursing, S.S. Hospital, Baroda 1.025\n2 Jharkhand 3. School of Nursing, Mahatma Gandhi Memorial\nMedical College Hospital, Jamshedpur.\n5.065\n4. School of Nursing, Patliputra Medical College and\nHospital Dhanbad.\n2.025\n5. School of Nursing, Rajendra Institute of Medical\nSciences, Nurses Hostel, Bariatu, Ranchi\n1.025\n3 Himachal\nPradesh\n6. GNM Training Cent