    "ls|LS17_S15_U_145": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nDEPARTMENTOF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 145\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 02nd FEBRUARY, 2024\nNIKSHAY POSHAN YOJANA\n#145. SHRI SAUMITRA KHAN:\nSHRI JUGAL KISHORE SHARMA:\nSHRI RAMESH CHANDER KAUSHIK:\nSHRIMATI NA VNEETRA VIRANA:\nSHRI SUNIL KUMAR PINTU:\nSHRIMATI RAMA DEVI:\nSHRIMATI GEETAKORA:\nSHRI AJAYKUMAR MANDAL:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has taken/proposes to take measures to monitor and evaluate the\nutilisation of funds allocated to improve the nutritional status of Tuberculosis (TB) patients under\nthe Nikshay Poshan Yojana (NPY) in the country and if so, the details thereof;\n(b) the total budgetary allocation made under the said Yojana particularly for providing nutritional\nsupport to TB patients in Sonipat, Amravati, Sitamarhi, Sheohar, Bhagalpur, Jammu, Singhbhum\nand Bishnupur Parliamentary Constituencies of Haryana, Maharashtra, Bihar, Jammu & Kashmir,\nJharkhand and West Bengal respectively;\n(c) the details of the funds distributed/disbursed to ensure that TB patients receive adequate\nnutritional support under the said Yojana; and\n(d) the total number of beneficiaries under the said Yojana in the States of Haryana, Bihar, Jammu\n& Kashmir, Jharkhand and West Bengal, district-wise and State/UTs-wise?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF THE STATEIN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY\nWELFARE\n(DR. BHARATI PRA VINPAWAR)\n(a) to (c) The Government under National TB Elimination Programme (NTEP) introduced Ni-\nkshay Poshan Yojana (NPY) in April 2018 to provide Rs 500/month for the duration of\ntreatment, as Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) to support nutrition of TB patients. The\nGovernment monitors the allocation and utilization of funds under Ni-kshay Poshan Yojana\n(NPY) on regular basis at national & State/UT levels. The mechanism for monitoring and\nevaluation of NPY includes: -\n Common Review Mission visits of National Health Mission (NHM)\n Supportive Supervisory Field Visits to state & districts by program division\n\n Review by National Programme Coordination Committee\n Real-time monitoring is done through dashboards in Ni-kshay portal.\nThe total budgetary allocation for Ni-kshay Poshan Yojana to provide nutritional support to TB\npatients in country for 2021-22, 2022-23 and 2023-24 is Rs 680.74 crores, Rs. 777.39 crores & Rs.\n766.89 crores respectively. The States of Haryana, Maharashtra, Bihar, Jammu & Kashmir\nJharkhand and West Bengal have been allocated Rs 177.83 crores, Rs 194.11 crores in 2022 and\nRs 198.65 crores in 2023.\nThe details of fund disbursed and beneficiaries paid (as per Ni-kshay portal) in Sonipat, Amravati,\nSitamarhi, Sheohar, Bhagalpur, Jammu, Singhbhum and Bishnupur NTEP district in 2022 and 2023\n(Jan - Dec) are as under:\nState NTEP\nDistrict\n2021 (Jan – Dec) 2022 (Jan – Dec) 2023 (Jan – Dec)\nBeneficiarie\ns paid (in\nNo's)\nFund\ndisbursed\n(Rs in\nlakh)\nBeneficiarie\ns paid (in\nNo's)\nFund\ndisbursed\n(Rs in\nlakh)\nBeneficiarie\ns paid (in\nNo's)\nFund\ndisbursed\n(Rs in\nlakh)\nBihar\nSitamarhi 1999 58.27 3284 84.12 1696 37.57\nSheohar 520 15.16 740 20.68 487 11.39\nBhagalpur 4682 149.45 5795 149.00 4760 88.51\nHaryana Sonipat 3521 101.28 3796 115.01 3454 86.20\nMaharashtr\na\nAmravati 1967 53.97 2551 75.10 1695 43.02\nAmravati\nMC 865 25.44 1183 34.79 914 22.75\nJammu &\nKashmir Jammu 2232 58.38 2450 64.08 2086 46.29\nJharkhand\nPashchimi\nSinghbhum 2638 73.53 3072 84.37 2835 69.08\nPurbi\nSinghbhum 3875 115.65 4270 126.19 4615 105.80\nWest\nBengal Bishnupur 1050 30.22 1069 25.54 515 5.55\n(d) ) The State/UTs wise details of total number of beneficiaries under the Ni-kshay Poshan Yojana\n(NPY) for last 3 years, is placed as Annexure-I and district wise details for Haryana, Bihar,\nJammu & Kashmir, Jharkhand and West Bengal, in last 3 calendar years is placed as Annexure-II.\n\nAnnexure-I\n1. State